WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.220
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:03.870
- Some property developers in China

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:07.098
are going to great lengths
to attract home buyers.

00:00:07.098 --> 00:00:09.180
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:12.600
One offered cars and
parking spots as a gift,

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:15.480
while another promised to
give the buyer a Mercedes-Benz

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:16.983
with the purchase of a villa.

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:20.520
One developer even
offered to accept garlic

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.500
as part of the down payment.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:26.250
The ads suggest that for
Chinese property developers,

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:28.500
demand is down.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:30.060
Since the summer of last year,

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:33.240
home sales for China's 100
biggest property developers

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:34.320
have tumbled.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:37.080
Home sales, of course, are
not just struggling in China,

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:38.790
in the Western world as well.

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:40.020
Home sales have been under pressure

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:42.090
after record surge in prices.

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:43.800
Inflation has become a problem

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:46.350
and fears of a recession are growing.

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:49.470
But in China, there are a
number of different factors,

00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:51.660
including concerns about the debt levels

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:52.800
of property developers,

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:55.290
as well as COVID 19 lockdowns.

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:57.270
China is the world's
second largest economy,

00:00:57.270 --> 00:00:58.290
so anything that happens

00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:01.290
within its own borders
and in its own economy

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:03.150
has ripple effects for
the rest of the world.

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:05.340
So here's how the government
and property developers

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:08.013
are rolling out measures
to help boost home sales.

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:11.910
China's real estate market has become

00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:14.220
perhaps the most important industry of all

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:15.480
in China's economy.

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:18.540
The estimates tend to be
that the real estate market

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:20.610
accounting for between 25%

00:01:20.610 --> 00:01:22.950
even up to one third of China's economy.

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:27.060
Home prices had just gone up
every year for several decades.

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:29.490
It also enriched a lot
of property developers

00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:32.460
and had them trying to
race ahead of one another

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:36.210
to buy more land and to
bring in more presales

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:37.770
so that they could fill their coffers

00:01:37.770 --> 00:01:40.170
and buy ever more land.

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:43.380
And that model was perhaps
most clearly exemplified

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:45.210
by a company called Evergrande,

00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:47.670
that is one of the country's
biggest property companies

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:49.470
as well as one of the most indebted,

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:52.500
it quickly found itself pushed
to the brink of collapse.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:54.870
Chinese regulators last year began to take

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:58.500
the most concrete steps
that they have taken yet

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:02.050
to try and curb developers' debt levels.

00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:04.230
(protesters speaking in foreign language)

00:02:04.230 --> 00:02:05.880
That created a crisis at Evergrande,

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:08.250
which jolted consumer
confidence in the market,

00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:10.890
causing concerns about
China's economic growth

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:12.750
as well as whether other
real estate companies

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:13.593
could fall too.

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:16.890
In addition to the regulatory pressures,

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:19.200
developers also faced another foe

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:21.570
in the form of COVID 19 lockdowns.

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:23.040
It kept potential home buyers

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:26.460
in many cities and provinces
across China, home bound.

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:30.120
So both property developers and
Chinese government officials

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:31.470
have started to take some steps

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:34.290
to arrest the slide in home prices,

00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:37.230
and maybe even to perk
them up a little bit.

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:40.380
On the government side,
officials in dozens of cities

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:42.360
and other jurisdictions across the country

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:43.680
lowered mortgage rates

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:46.260
and made it easier to buy an apartment,

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:48.300
if you're young and on the market.

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:50.070
Meanwhile, among property developers,

00:02:50.070 --> 00:02:52.710
they're advertising free
gifts with a home purchase.

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:55.170
Some have gone to even
more creative measures.

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:58.410
For example, one company is
giving out an actual pig,

00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:00.693
while another is offering
job opportunities.

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:04.110
The response from the Chinese
public has been mixed.

00:03:04.110 --> 00:03:06.300
If you look online,
you'll find some comments

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:09.390
that talk about interest
in buying an apartment,

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:11.670
but you also see some
skepticism online too.

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:14.100
It does seem gimmicky to some people,

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:15.690
and for many people,

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:18.000
the question is whether
or not they feel confident

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:19.700
going out and buying an apartment.

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:21.810
The real question, of course,

00:03:21.810 --> 00:03:24.090
is how effective these policies can be.

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:28.740
It's probably gonna rely more
on big macroeconomic factors

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:31.950
rather than on what freebies
developers throw in,

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:34.320
or what incremental loosening measures

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:37.440
one's city or town has.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:38.310
To build at the pace

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:41.220
that China has been building
at for the last few years

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:44.610
consumed a vast quantity of inputs

00:03:44.610 --> 00:03:47.280
that were acquired from
outside of the country.

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:49.680
So any sharp slowdown
that we see in housing

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:53.160
is gonna have impact on
commodity producing countries

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:54.300
all around the world.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.670
And so that is something

00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:58.830
that people all around the
world are gonna be watching,

00:03:58.830 --> 00:04:01.200
whether the Chinese home buyer comes back,

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:03.800
and whether these developers
survive and thrive.

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:06.383
(bright music)

